      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just a heads up, but probably not this CLs fault.\n\nWhen trying to compile for an stm32f0 chip (I\u0027m using the nucleo-f072 board) you\u0027ll get errors such as:\naccelgyro_lsm6dsm.c:342: undefined reference to `__ctzsi2\u0027\n\n\nI actually had to implement __ctzsi2 in common/clz.c in order to overcome this:\n/**\n * Count trailing zeros\n *\n * @param x non null integer.\n * @return the number of trailing 0-bits in x,\n * starting at the most significant bit position.\n */\nint __keep __ctzsi2(int x)\n{\n\tint r \u003d 0;\n\n\tif (!x)\n\t\treturn 32;\n\tif (!(x \u0026 0x0000ffffu)) {\n\t\tx \u003e\u003e\u003d 16;\n\t\tr +\u003d 16;\n\t}\n\tif (!(x \u0026 0x000000FFu)) {\n\t\tx \u003e\u003e\u003d 8;\n\t\tr +\u003d 8;\n\t}\n\tif (!(x \u0026 0x0000000Fu)) {\n\t\tx \u003e\u003e\u003d 4;\n\t\tr +\u003d 4;\n\t}\n\tif (!(x \u0026 0x00000003u)) {\n\t\tx \u003e\u003e\u003d 2;\n\t\tr +\u003d 2;\n\t}\n\tif (!(x \u0026 0x00000001u)) {\n\t\tx \u003e\u003e\u003d 1;\n\t\tr +\u003d 1;\n\t}\n\treturn r;\n}",
